    {
      "section": "article.story-header",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "logo": {
          "assetRole": "customer.logo",
          "alt": "Kestrel",
          "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-1.svg"
        },
        "title": "Kestrel halves its nightly build time and gives store managers fresh numbers before the morning shift begins",
        "stats": [
          {
            "value": "52%",
            "label": "shorter nightly runs"
          },
          {
            "value": "400+",
            "label": "production models on state-aware builds"
          },
          {
            "value": "3.2x",
            "label": "more models shipped per sprint"
          }
        ],
        "quote": "Our nightly load used to finish after stand-up, so nobody trusted the first dashboards of the day. Now every number is ready before anyone logs on.",
        "name": "Priya Raman",
        "role": "Head of Analytics Engineering"
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "stroke.draw-on",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "render-final-state"
      },
      "style": {
        "strokeShape": "stroke.s10",
        "strokeGradient": "gradient.01"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "article.story-body",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "meta": {
          "logo": {
            "assetRole": "customer.logo",
            "alt": "Kestrel",
            "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-1.svg"
          },
          "facts": [
            {
              "label": "Industry",
              "value": "Food and grocery retail"
            },
            {
              "label": "Headquarters",
              "value": "Copenhagen, Denmark"
            },
            {
              "label": "Stores",
              "value": "310 across four countries"
            },
            {
              "label": "Data platform and tools used",
              "value": "Cobalt DB, Lattice, Driftway connectors"
            }
          ]
        },
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "A grocery chain that runs on early-morning numbers"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Kestrel operates more than three hundred grocery stores across four Nordic countries. Store managers plan staffing, deliveries and markdowns every morning based on the previous day’s sales, stock and waste figures."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Those figures came from a nightly batch that rebuilt the entire warehouse from scratch. As the business grew, the batch grew with it, until it regularly finished after stores had already opened."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Managers started making decisions on numbers that were a day older than they thought, and the data team spent its mornings explaining delays instead of building anything new."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Fresh produce makes the timing even more important. A markdown decided an hour late can mean a crate of berries thrown away instead of sold, and across three hundred stores those hours add up to real money and real waste."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "The cost of rebuilding everything every night"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Most of the work in the nightly batch was wasted. Only a small share of source tables changed on a typical day, yet every model was rebuilt regardless, which made the job slow and expensive."
          },
          {
            "kind": "ul",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "Nightly runs took more than six hours and often failed late in the process."
              },
              {
                "text": "Warehouse costs grew faster than sales for two years in a row."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The team had tried to speed things up with bigger warehouse settings and by splitting the batch into stages. Each fix helped for a few months, until data volumes caught up again and the runs slipped back past opening time."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Rebuilding only what changed"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Kestrel moved its project to Lattice and switched on state-aware builds for production. Before each run, Lattice now checks which sources and models have changed since the last successful build and skips everything else."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "On a normal night, fewer than half of the models need rebuilding. The rest are reused as they are."
          },
          {
            "kind": "img",
            "image": {
              "assetRole": "figure.article-image",
              "alt": "Diagram: nightly full reloads replaced by state-aware builds",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/story/kestrel-flow.svg"
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The switch itself took a few weeks. Most of that time went into tidying up models that depended on the current date or on tables outside the project, which made it hard to tell whether their inputs had really changed."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "Freshness rules instead of a fixed schedule"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The team also replaced the single nightly schedule with freshness rules. Sales models rebuild as soon as till data lands; slower-moving reference data rebuilds once a week."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Event-based triggers mean the morning numbers are ready the moment their inputs land, not at a fixed hour picked years ago."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Each freshness rule was agreed with the people who use the figures. Store operations wanted sales by six in the morning; the buying team was happy with supplier data refreshed twice a day."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Faster runs, fewer failures"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Nightly runs now finish in about half the time, and most mornings the store dashboards are ready well before the first shift starts."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Because each run does less work, failures are rarer and much easier to diagnose. When something does break, only the affected models need to be rerun."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The on-call rotation got quieter as well. In the quarter before the move the team was paged for a failed run almost every week; in the quarter after, it happened twice."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "A smaller bill for the same results"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Warehouse spend dropped by roughly a third in the first quarter after the switch, with no reports removed and no changes to the questions the business asks."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Finance now receives a monthly breakdown of spend by model and by business area, which has made budget conversations shorter and far less tense than they used to be."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "Tests where they matter most"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "With time freed up, the team added tests on the figures store managers rely on most: stock levels never negative, markdowns never above list price and every store reporting every day."
          },
          {
            "kind": "ul",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "Freshness checks on every till feed."
              },
              {
                "text": "Reconciliation tests between sales and stock movements."
              },
              {
                "text": "Alerts routed to the owner of each regional mart."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "More models, shipped with confidence"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Faster builds made development faster too. Continuous integration runs only the changed models and their dependants, so a pull request gets feedback in minutes rather than hours."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The team now ships more than three times as many models per sprint as it did before the move, without any increase in incidents."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "New analysts productive in a week"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Documentation and examples live next to the code, and every change is reviewed. New analysts ship their first production model within a week of joining."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "“The project explains itself now,” says Priya Raman, Head of Analytics Engineering. “That used to be my job.”"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Each newcomer starts with a small, well-scoped change chosen in advance, paired with a reviewer who knows that part of the project well. By the end of the week they have shipped something real and know where to look for help."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "What comes next"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Kestrel is extending the same approach to its supply chain data, where faster and cheaper builds could support intraday replenishment decisions."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "Metrics for every store"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The team is also moving its key store metrics into the semantic layer, so that store dashboards, finance reports and a planned assistant for store managers all read the same definitions."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The goal for next year is simple: every number a store manager sees in the morning is tested, documented and ready on time."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Store managers were involved from the start. A small group of them reviewed draft metric definitions and pointed out several cases, such as stores that close for a season, that the data team had not considered."
          }
        ]
      },
